Problem
Assemble a clean order report by splitting packed name and product fields.

You are a data analyst at the multinational flooring retailer Floors'R'Us. The sales system exports customer names as a single full_name string and product attributes packed into a comma-separated product_info string. The sales team wants one tidy row per order with the name and product attributes split into separate fields.

Build one row per order, combining each order with its customer's and product's details; orders without a matching customer and product are dropped.
Derive first_name and last_name by splitting full_name on the single space (first part and second part).
Derive product_type and product_color by splitting product_info on the comma (first part and second part).
Return the columns in exactly this order: customer_id, first_name, last_name, location, order_id, product_type, product_color, product_id, quantity, with rows in ascending order of order_id.
Output columns: customer_id, first_name, last_name, location, order_id, product_type, product_color, product_id, quantity


